# Byte-exact golden fixtures must reach the working tree unmodified.
#
# Without this, a Windows clone with the default `core.autocrlf=true` rewrites
# every LF to CRLF on checkout. The persisted formats are unaffected -- these
# are text renderings of golden bytes, not the bytes themselves -- but a golden
# compared as a whole string then differs from what the engine renders, and the
# test fails for a reason that has nothing to do with the engine.
crates/zeppelin-embed/tests/fixtures/** -text

# Shell scripts must stay LF so they remain executable when a Windows checkout
# is used from WSL, Git Bash or a container.
*.sh text eol=lf
